How the old GUI drew at all (needed for every style row below)
    ⚠ The reference copy and Bot draw by DIFFERENT roads, and neither is
    native drawing of the field tree:
        Groups/GUI   Layout.twk drawRect 119-155 lays out, then builds an
                     HTML page with a <canvas> (Control.twk makeCanvas 402,
                     jsDraw 953-1040 writes one drawBox(...) JS call per
                     field) and loads it into a WKWebView. Fonts, alignment,
                     margins, flex etc. go out as CSS through toCSS (915) and
                     the CSS / pROPERTIEs registries in
                     IncantForms/HTML/htmlTraits.
        Bot          Layout.twk drawRect 28-70 renders the laid-out tree to a
                     PDF (Bot/PDF.twk, 523 lines: drawRoundedBox, displayCell,
                     displayImage, displayPath, getFontFrom, setPDFfill /
                     setPDFstroke) and shows it in a PDFView. That is the
                     "print-driven layout" Tony's forms notes propose -- Bot
                     already did it, in 2021.
    Layout itself (Control layout, Details setFrame / checkStretch /
    setInnerBox / checkFit) is the same in both and is plain arithmetic.

